  "extractionNotes": "ZUS memo lists sickness benefit 2023-12-13..2024-02-15 and the maternity claim 2024-02-16..2025-02-13; the closing note says all benefits (sickness and maternity for maternity + parental leave from the same mandate contract) were granted and paid. The maternity/parental split is the claim (ZAM). Declared sickness bases from the ZUS memo: 235.00 for 2023-07 (insured from 2023-07-14) and 940.00 for 2023-08..2023-11; the payer's Z-3a shows 940 for 2023-07 in one copy and 235 in another. ZUS letter: the maternity benefit net of tax is below 1000 zl, so a top-up to the parental-benefit level is paid from February 2024 (art. 31 ust. 3a cited there). The 81.5% box on the ZAM appears unticked although both periods were claimed together within 21 days of the birth, so averaged81_5 is inferred and no rate is asserted. Sickness code B (pregnancy) inferred from the sickness ending the day before the birth. Birth date inferred from the start of the maternity claim (birth extract date illegible). 90-day voluntary waiting period met (insured 2023-07-14, sick 2023-12-13). singleTitleStatement set to true: the top-up was paid, which requires the single-title statement (added during engine triage)."
